{"i":502,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Cole","text":"Gus lied before, but the pattern is not reliable. Row 8 is a fresh row. I need to counter based on my own read—probably L, matching his call? Wait, he said L after lying last time. But the past rows: R at 4-6, L at 7. No clear pattern. I'll trust that Gus might be telling truth n"}
{"i":504,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Dara","text":"Gus is a known liar who betrayed Fenn. His call for L is suspicious, especially since he steered Fenn wrong. However, Gus has no motive to lie if the prize is guaranteed; but in Last Three, he might try to eliminate me to reduce competition or save himself from jury backlash by p"}
